### What is idiomatic Optional usage?

Never use isPresent()+get(). Use the functional API: map, flatMap, filter, orElse, orElseThrow, ifPresent.

### How do you use map for transformations?

```java
package com.bank.service;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.Optional;

public class IdiomaticOptional {
    record Account(String id, String holder, BigDecimal balance, boolean active) {
        Optional<String> getMiddleName() { return Optional.empty(); }
    }

    static Optional<Account> findAccount(String id) {
        if ("SAV2001".equals(id)) {
            return Optional.of(new Account("SAV2001", "Rajesh", new BigDecimal("125000"), true));
        }
        return Optional.empty();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // map: transform if present, empty if absent
        String name = findAccount("SAV2001")
            .map(Account::holder)
            .map(String::toUpperCase)
            .orElse("UNKNOWN");
        System.out.println("Name: " + name); // RAJESH
    }
}
```

### How do you use filter for conditions?

```java
// filter: keep only if active
BigDecimal balance = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .filter(Account::active)
    .map(Account::balance)
    .orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO);
System.out.println("Active balance: Rs." + balance); // Rs.125000
```

### How do you use flatMap to avoid nested Optionals?

```java
// flatMap: avoid nested Optional<Optional<T>>
String middle = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .flatMap(Account::getMiddleName) // returns Optional, flatMap unwraps
    .orElse("N/A");
System.out.println("Middle name: " + middle); // N/A

// Without flatMap: map would produce Optional<Optional<String>>
// Optional<Optional<String>> nested = findAccount("SAV2001").map(Account::getMiddleName);
// flatMap flattens it to Optional<String>
```

### How do you use ifPresent and ifPresentOrElse?

```java
// ifPresent: action only when present
findAccount("SAV2001")
    .ifPresent(a -> System.out.println("Found: " + a.holder()));

// ifPresentOrElse (Java 9): handle both cases
findAccount("SAV9999")
    .ifPresentOrElse(
        a -> System.out.println("Found: " + a.holder()),
        () -> System.out.println("Account not found")
    );
```

### How do you use orElse, orElseGet, and orElseThrow?

```java
// orElse: cheap default (eager)
String name = findAccount("SAV9999")
    .map(Account::holder)
    .orElse("Unknown");

// orElseGet: expensive default (lazy)
Account account = findAccount("SAV9999")
    .orElseGet(() -> repository.loadFromBackup("SAV9999"));

// orElseThrow: required value
Account account = findAccount("SAV9999")
    .orElseThrow(() -> new AccountNotFoundException("SAV9999"));
```

### How do you chain a complete pipeline?

```java
// Complete null-safe pipeline: zero null checks
String result = findAccount(accountId)
    .filter(Account::active)
    .flatMap(Account::getMiddleName)
    .map(String::toUpperCase)
    .orElse("N/A");
```

### What is the anti-pattern comparison?

| Anti-pattern | Idiomatic |
|-------------|----------|
| `if (opt.isPresent()) opt.get()` | `opt.ifPresent(action)` |
| `opt.isPresent() ? opt.get().name() : "default"` | `opt.map(T::name).orElse("default")` |
| `opt.isPresent() ? opt.get() : computeDefault()` | `opt.orElseGet(() -> computeDefault())` |
| `if (!opt.isPresent()) throw new Ex()` | `opt.orElseThrow(() -> new Ex())` |

### What should a senior engineer know?

- flatMap is needed when the mapping function itself returns Optional. map wraps the result in Optional (producing nested Optional<Optional<T>>). flatMap returns the result directly.
- This parallels Stream.flatMap exactly.
- Optional.stream() (Java 9) bridges Optional and Stream: `optionals.stream().flatMap(Optional::stream)` removes empties.
- In code reviews, flag any isPresent()+get() as a code smell.
